  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Supplycore has $461M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Supplycore has 23,323 awards this fiscal year to date, with an average award size of $19.7K. Supplycore obligations are down 43.7% year over year. Supplycore obligations by fiscal year show $265M in FY21, $356M in FY22, $527M in FY23, $592M in FY24, $818M in FY25, and $461M in FY26. Supplycore receives most of its FY2026 obligations from the Department of Defense, which has $443M in obligations to Supplycore. Supplycore also has $17.3M in obligations from the General Services Administration and $219K from the Department of Justice. Supplycore sells a mix of manufactured goods and wholesale items to the government, led by All Other Miscellaneous Manufacturing at $146M and Bare Printed Circuit Board Manufacturing at $141M, followed by Service Establishment Equipment and Supplies Merchant Wholesalers at $104M. Supplycore figures for the current year are partial because the totals are fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are Supplycore's top federal buyers?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is Supplycore's top buyer with $443M in obligations. The General Services Administration has $17.3M in obligations to Supplycore. The Department of Justice has $219K in obligations to Supplycore."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and products drive Supplycore's federal revenue?",
        "body": "All Other Miscellaneous Manufacturing accounts for $146M of Supplycore's FY2026 obligations. Bare Printed Circuit Board Manufacturing accounts for $141M and Service Establishment Equipment and Supplies Merchant Wholesalers accounts for $104M. Other notable markets for Supplycore include Electrical Apparatus and Equipment, Wiring Supplies, and Related Equipment Merchant Wholesalers at $38.1M and Other Warehousing and Storage at $17.3M."
      }
    ]
  },
